  "notes": "Interleaved two-block extraction (Bravyi et al. arXiv:2308.07915 Table 5 style): joint reset and measurement layers, 9 CX layers per round; X-check term slots [1, 7, 8, 4, 5, 3, 2, 6], Z-check term slots [7, 1, 0, 2, 6, 4, 5, 3] over terms A_0..A_2, B_0..B_4; terms recovered from H alone by a commuting permutation decomposition; circuits generated by research/circuit_autogen.py (seed 0, the first of up to 6 candidates whose RIS screen at 2 rounds found nothing below d). The recorded witnesses are not from RIS (which finds nothing below weight 37 at this size) but constructed: a single ancilla hook, the cheapest completion of its remaining-support error to a logical (exact oracle up to weight 8) placed at the start or end of the last round, and one measurement flip per check that still sees the partial error; 9 faults in each basis, checked in GF(2). Multi-hook combinations were not analysed, so d_circ <= 9 is an upper bound that a stronger search may lower.",
